{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["A Canaanite — as its Targum renders: 'a merchant.' As in: ״כנעניה נכבדי ארץ״; ״כנען בידו מאזני מרמה״ — for they were careful [to marry] from among the daughters of Canaan."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashbam, :lang :en, :chapter 38, :notes {0 "The final clause כי מבנות כנען היו נזהרין is textually uncertain; rendered hyper-literally. It may mean the Canaanites were careful about marrying their own daughters, or that others were careful to marry Canaanite daughters."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:46:34.605600069Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}